.TH SCHEMA-REVERSE 1 "2026 July 10" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
schema\-reverse \- reverse-engineer databases to data-schema documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B schema\-reverse
[\fIoptions\fP]
\fIconnection\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBschema\-reverse\fR connects to a database and generates a complete Qore
data-schema document in YAML (\fB.ysm\fP) or JSON (\fB.jsm\fP) format.
It supports tables, sequences, materialized views, types, functions,
procedures, and packages.
Plain views cannot be exported because the data-schema format has no
representation for them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-schema =\fIname\fP
Set the schema name in the output (default: \fBExportedSchema\fP).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIfile\fP
Write the data-schema document to \fIfile\fP instead of standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-format =\fIformat\fP
Set the output format to \fByaml\fP (default) or \fBjson\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-with\-partitions
Include physical table partitions in the export.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-table [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching tables.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-seq [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching sequences.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-type [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching types.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mview [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching materialized views.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-proc [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching procedures.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-func [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching functions.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-pkg [=\fIpattern\fP]
Export matching packages.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable colored status output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Write verbose status output to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.PP
Each object-selection \fIpattern\fP can be an exact name, a comma-separated
list, or a regular expression.
A selection option without a value selects all objects of that type.
Selection options can be combined; if none is given, the whole schema is
exported.
.SH EXAMPLES
Export the full schema to a YAML file:
.RS
.B schema\-reverse \-s MySchema pgsql:user/pass@db \-o myschema.ysm
.RE
.PP
Export specific tables as JSON:
.RS
.B schema\-reverse \-\-table='workflows,.*step.*' \-\-format json mydb
.RE
.PP
Include physical partitions:
.RS
.B schema\-reverse \-\-with\-partitions oracle:user/pass@tns
.RE
